===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# Work, especially [[research]] or [[preparation]], that involves [[significant]] [[walking]], [[travel]], or similar [[effort]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=7 Mar 1955|title=Who'll Buy My Stocks?|titleurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20081215040734/http://www.time.com/time/magazine/article/0,9171,861334,00.html|journal=Time
|passage=In addition to spreading more information, brokers are going to have to do some '''leg work''' to get new customers.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=1 May 2003|author=Peter Spotts|title=What the world has done right on SARS|titleurl=http://www.csmonitor.com/2003/0501/p01s01-wogi.html|journal=Christian Science Monitor|accessdate=5 Jan. 2009
|passage=The worldwide effort has already revealed several valuable lessons [including] . . . the use of old-fashioned '''legwork''' in tracking down people who may unknowingly carry a virus.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2004|author=Jerry Acuff|title=The Relationship Edge in Business|page=62
|passage=John did all the '''legwork'''. He had the invitations printed and mailed. He found speakers.}}
# [[skillful|Skillful]] or [[vigorous]] use of the legs, as in [[dance]] or [[sport]]s.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=11 May 1890|title=Atalanta and Yale Race: An English expert criticizes the crews of Yale and Harvard|titleurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20160306203500/http://query.nytimes.com/mem/archive-free/pdf?res=9806E3DD123BE533A25752C1A9639C94619ED7CF|journal=New York Times|accessdate=5 Jan 2009|page=20
|passage="Watriss, No. 3, is rowing well. . . . His '''leg work''' is very fair."}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2005|author=Thomas Incledon; Matthew Hoffman|title=Men's Health Maximum Muscle Plan|page=353
|passage=Fancy '''legwork''' and jumping rope will get you in great shape.}}

